  "summary": "About nine Hartford, Wisconsin residents urged the city council to remove four Flock Safety ALPR cameras on public roads, calling them a 'warrantless mass surveillance dragnet.' Hartford Police defended their ethical use of the cameras, and the council took no action.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "These cameras operate as a warrantless mass surveillance dragnet that treats every law abiding citizen like a suspect",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Hartford has five Flock cameras in total \u2014 four used by the city on public roads and one owned and used by Walmart.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "The city council did not take any action or say whether it will consider removing the cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
